{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nA container ticket (epic/story with children) rarely declares its own `file_impact`, so its\nplan-review attestation's signed dependency set is empty and the code-drift gate falls back to\nwhole-HEAD invalidation (ADR 0002 decision 5): ANY commit — however unrelated — invalidates the\ncontainer's attestation, forcing a re-review or drift-refresh on every merge. This is the\ncontainer-scale form of the over-invalidation ADR 0002 was written to fix, and a real\ngate-economics drag under the parallel epic/child workflow where the base ref moves constantly.\n\nThe scope a container plan actually reasons about is its children's declared scope. The\ninvalidation lattice for inheritance already exists: `material_fingerprint` (pass1.py:551)\nhashes a ticket's description + file_impact + child ids, and a container review pins each\nDIRECT child's material fingerprint into the signed manifest — so a child editing its\nfile_impact (or a child being added/removed) already invalidates the container's attestation\nvia pin/material drift, forcing a re-review that recomputes any inherited union. Inheritance\ntherefore cannot go silently stale one level deep. It does NOT hold for grandchildren (a\nchild's fingerprint covers grandchild IDS only, not grandchild file_impact), which is why\ninheritance is DIRECT CHILDREN ONLY — deeper drift is covered by the deeper tickets' own\nattestations, mirroring the review model (reviews pin direct dependencies; dependency-order\nreview covers each tier).\n\nDepends on 72d9-8fbd (athletic-esthetical-polecat) landing first: before that fix, scoped\ndependency sets are inert in attested mode, so giving containers a non-empty set would move\nthem OFF the only working invalidation (whole-HEAD) onto a broken path.\n\n## Approach\n1. In `dependency_hashes` (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py): when the reviewed ticket\n   has children, compute the candidate union = own `file_impact` ∪ review citations ∪ the\n   union of DIRECT children's `file_impact`. Apply the POISON RULE: if any non-closed direct\n   child has an empty `file_impact`, do NOT inherit — keep the pre-change set (own ∪\n   citations; empty ⇒ whole-HEAD fallback), preserving fail-closed for undeclared scope.\n   Closed children neither contribute files nor poison (their work is delivered; ADR 0024's\n   completion floor deliberately stops re-litigating it, and their files' later churn belongs\n   to other tickets). Child ids/statuses come from the same light store reads\n   `attest.current_material_fingerprint` uses; child file_impact via `rebar.get_file_impact`.\n   Read failures keep the pre-change behavior (fail-closed to whole-HEAD), logged.\n2. Extend P9 (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_floor.py, `p9_file_impact_coverage`): containers\n   currently auto-pass. Keep passing when inheritance is effective (every non-closed direct\n   child declares file_impact, and there is at least one). Surface an ADVISORY (never\n   blocking) on a container whose inheritance is poisoned, naming the children with empty\n   file_impact, so authors see exactly why the epic stays on whole-HEAD invalidation. Leaf\n   behavior unchanged.\n3. Document: docs/plan-review-gate.md (scoped-drift paragraph: containers inherit direct\n   children's declared impact under the poison rule) and a short amendment note in\n   docs/adr/0002-code-drift-invalidation.md decision 5.\nRejected: recursive (whole-subtree) inheritance — the pin lattice only self-heals one level\ndeep, so a grandchild file_impact edit would leave a recursively-computed union silently\nstale. Rejected: inheriting a partial union when some children lack file_impact — that flips\nthe empty-set fallback from fail-closed to fail-open for exactly the undeclared portion.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py (dependency_hashes + a small child-union helper)\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_floor.py (P9 container extension)\n- tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_review_gate.py\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review.py (the existing P9 unit tests pin the old container auto-pass\n  and must be updated to the new container semantics)\n- docs/plan-review-gate.md, docs/adr/0002-code-drift-invalidation.md\n\n## Testing\nInterface tests in tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_review_gate.py against a tmp repo with\nthe suite's attested/ref=HEAD default, committing drift via the existing `_commit_all` helper:\ncontainer+children fixtures asserting the signed manifest's `dep` paths (inherited union,\npoison rule, closed-child exclusion), claim-gate outcomes (unrelated commit keeps the claim\nopen; a committed change to a child-declared file blocks the claim naming drift), the\nchild-file_impact-edit → container pin invalidation property, and DET-floor unit assertions\nfor the P9 container advisory. In tests/unit/test_plan_review.py, replace\ntest_p9_not_applicable_for_container (which asserts the old unconditional container pass)\nwith three container cases: effective inheritance passes, a non-closed impact-less child\nyields the poisoning advisory naming the child id, and a closed impact-less child does not\npoison; leaf cases unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A container whose non-closed direct children all declare non-empty file_impact signs a\n      dependency set equal to own file_impact ∪ citations ∪ the children's union — asserted\n      by parsing `dep` lines from the signed manifest in an interface test.\n- [ ] Poison rule: if any non-closed direct child has empty file_impact, the signed set is\n      unchanged from pre-change behavior (empty ⇒ whole-HEAD fallback applies) — asserted by\n      manifest inspection plus a claim blocked after an unrelated commit.\n- [ ] Closed children neither contribute paths nor poison the union — asserted with a fixture\n      containing one closed impact-less child.\n- [ ] With inheritance effective: an unrelated committed change does NOT invalidate the\n      container attestation (claim succeeds); a committed change to a child-declared file\n      DOES (claim blocked, reason names drift) — both asserted via rebar.claim.\n- [ ] A child editing its file_impact after the container review invalidates the container's\n      attestation (pin/material drift) — asserted via claim_gate_check.\n- [ ] P9: a container with poisoned inheritance yields an advisory naming the offending\n      child id(s); a container with effective inheritance passes; leaf behavior is unchanged —\n      asserted in DET-floor tests.\n- [ ] docs/plan-review-gate.md and ADR 0002 describe container inheritance and the poison\n      rule.\n- [ ] make lint, make typecheck, and the default non-integration pytest suite exit zero."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785010937619037001,"uuid":"a56590a8-af92-47d8-a0df-0bd35e8f0161"}